# Fix from gate output (binding)

When `precommit`, husky, ESLint, TSC, or qualitygate **already printed** failing paths and line numbers:

## Do

1. **Fix the named files** — real fixes only.
2. Re-run the **same gate once** to confirm.
3. Continue the original user goal (commit, push, etc.).

**IMPORTANT — never disable rules on your own if not allowed.** Gate pressure is not approval to turn rules off in `eslint.config.js` or sprinkle `eslint-disable`. Ask first (`no-gate-bypass.mdc`).

## Do not

- Re-run eslint/tsc in “count by file / uniq / tally / inventory” loops.
- Write aggregators (`awk`, `uniq -c`, JSON reporters) to rediscover what the log already said.
- Spend turns classifying severity while the fix is obvious (e.g. `e2e/**` magic-string → same override as `scripts/**` / `evals/**`).

## When the list is large

Use `.local/quality-backlog.md` (`qualitygate:capture`) — still **no** custom recount scripts. Work the backlog ids.

## Anti-pattern this kills

Gate says `vitest.config.ts:7 magic-string` → agent runs three more shells to “list unique files with errors” instead of editing `eslint.config.js` or the file.
